display_name="T6 Front Panel"
desc="Front touch-screen app for the UnifyDrive UP6 / ZSpace T6: dashboard, screen and network info, device settings. Requires T6 Control Center and Appliance Compositor."
changelog="2.0.1: the tab bar is now dark indigo cloth by day, with the current tab on a pale straw-yellow label, so it stands out from the page from across the room; at night the current tab is an indigo label. The status bar shows every connection in use side by side: Bluetooth, Wi-Fi or the hotspot, and wired. Settings › Screen has one Idle row that opens a page for dimming and turning the screen off. In English, the names of tabs behind in Files fade out instead of being cut mid-word. 2.0.0: a new look and layout, built on the Ridgeline design system: four tabs (Overview, Files, Network, Settings), a control center pulled down from the status bar, a status bar that shows the battery level and how many devices are on the hotspot, Chinese and English, and a light theme by default (dark is one tap away in Settings or the control center). Overview opens with a drawing of the NAS labelled with its processor, memory, temperature, network and storage readings, then shows storage, processor, memory, temperatures, network, containers, battery and notices, with charts over the last hour, day or week; the Storage page shows each volume's disks, a usage trend with an estimate of when it fills, and a disk check. Files: up to three tabs, shown as title slips, each keeping its own place (open a folder in a new tab from its menu); file icons in colour by type; signing out (or someone else signing in) closes the open folders and clears the clipboard and recent files; copies and moves run in the background with their progress in the status bar, pasting asks before replacing files with the same name, moving to the recycle bin can be undone, and the recycle bin can be emptied. Network: a connection map, Wi-Fi joins enterprise (802.1X) networks, the hotspot shows a QR code phones can scan to join, and the address sheet has a QR code that opens fnOS on a phone. Settings adds Sound and About pages and restarting just the panel; SSH asks before it changes. When idle the screen first dims (after 1–15 minutes, to 10, 25 or 50 % of its brightness; a touch brings it back) and later turns off (after 1, 12 or 24 hours, or never); the old screen timeout carries over as the dimming time. The remote's Home key steps through the four tabs. Japanese is no longer offered. 1.4.2: turning color correction on or off no longer restarts the screen; it is saved and applies after the NAS restarts. Restarting the screen could leave it black until a reboot. The Ethernet tile now shows any connected wired adapter, including USB ones, and the Ethernet page lists every adapter with its own IPv4 settings. 1.4.1: the screen and sound server now come from the new Appliance Compositor package, installed first and shared with other screen apps (such as Fygo Cinema on a TV); the panel, its video player and screensaver stay on the built-in screen. The on-screen keyboard's return key runs the Files search and closes the keyboard, instead of clicking whatever the focus ring was on. 1.4.0: remote and keyboard control: the arrow keys move a focus ring, OK opens, Back, Home and Menu work everywhere, and the volume keys set the volume, including in the video player. While the screen is dark it takes every key and touch: a key or a double tap wakes it, the volume keys don't. The screen fades to black before switching off and fades back in; a key during the fade cancels the switch-off. 1.3.0: a built-in video and music player (open a video or song in Files): hardware-decoded up to 4K HDR, touch controls, screen rotation, subtitles and a choice of audio output. Sound goes through PipeWire (installed automatically; installing is refused while PulseAudio is present): Settings → Audio picks the output and volume, and the admin page shows the sound server with an output choice and a Repair button. Settings → Bluetooth pairs headphones, speakers, keyboards, remotes and game controllers (keyboards show a pairing code) alongside the Bluetooth app; audio switches to a Bluetooth speaker when it connects. 1.2.0: Settings → Indicator lights has the full LED settings of the Control Center (bays, status LEDs, tray light, night mode with its daily window); brightness goes down to 1 %. 1.0.3: the screen timeout now runs in the backend and watches the touchscreen itself, so the screen still turns off if the panel app hangs or restarts; screen off no longer sleeps the panel (phantom touches, no double-tap wake). 1.0.2: panel sleep/wake with safe backlight ordering; display errors are reported without illuminating an uncertain panel; corrected kiosk start/stop sequencing."

